# Step 24 [vg_ism] (UE: Nanite instanced static meshes): a still ISM on a VG .stmesh is drawn ONCE into the VSM - by
# the cluster raster; the levels' CPU walk hides the field's clustered submeshes (ClusterWalkHidden over the field's
# primitive). Step 25: the sun cascades follow the same rule (MeshRenderer::ClusterWalkHidden, ShadowCascade pass):
# the field's cascade walk hides exactly its clustered submeshes and walks the rest - none twice, none lost.
# B16 has no ISM and one entity per mesh, so the field is made here: the table (step 21's) is duplicated
# in place ("Entity" "Duplicate selection", Ctrl+D's palette twin), both copies selected by mesh and collapsed into one
# ISM of two coincident instances (same depth as the one table, so VG off vs on compares like for like). The scene is
# not saved; the flag is turned off at the end.
Когда run Entity "Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Table_01___6__6503"
Когда run Entity "Duplicate selection"
Когда run Entity "Select all with the same static mesh"
Когда run Entity "Collapse selection into Instanced Static Mesh"
